DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 11

Docker (Basics + Advanced) | 0–2 Years Experience

Containers are the foundation of modern DevOps and Kubernetes.
Interviewers expect you to understand how Docker works internally, not just commands.

 Focus: Docker Interview Questions (Basics + Advanced)

• What is Docker and why is it used?
• Difference between virtualization and containerization
• Docker architecture (client, daemon, registry)
• What is a Docker image?
• What is a Docker container?
• Image vs container
• What is Dockerfile?
• Common Dockerfile instructions (FROM, RUN, COPY, CMD, ENTRYPOINT)
• Difference between CMD and ENTRYPOINT
• What is a Docker registry?
• Docker Hub vs private registry
• What is a Docker volume?
• Difference between volume and bind mount
• Docker networking basics
• Bridge vs host network
• What is Docker Compose?
• When do you use Docker Compose?

🔹 Advanced Docker Concepts

• What is a multi-stage Docker build?
• Why are multi-stage builds important?
• How do you reduce Docker image size?
• What are Docker layers and caching?
• What is .dockerignore?
• How do you scan Docker images for vulnerabilities?
• How do you pass secrets to Docker containers?
• Difference between ARG and ENV
• How do you troubleshoot a failing container?
• How do you monitor containers?
• Docker logging drivers
• How do you handle container restart policies?
• Common Docker mistakes beginners make
• Real-world Docker use case in DevOps pipeline

 Interview Tip:
If you can explain:
👉 “Dockerfile → Image → Container → Registry → Deploy”
you already sound like a job-ready DevOps engineer, even with 0–2 years of experience.
